{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/devin/repos/a2-ai/test-build-processes","sessionId":"07c0d90e-4e54-4832-897c-75001749ff8a","version":"2.0.22","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Your goal is to develop a release pipeline for github actions for this project, such that it builds for linux on aarch and x64. We have\n  many clients that use older systems so we want to build with alma8 for older glibc compatibility. Here is an approximate proposed github\n  release workflow. Start with a simpler version of this with just a single target in the matrix and get it working but work towards this concept. This example may not work correctly. To interact with github use the gh cli tool to monitor your steps and how the build is going. You may commit, push, pull from this repository ONLY.  To begin, come up with a plan for the incremental steps to take, and the success criteria for each step and approximately how you will assess success. I will review that, if it looks good, i will ask you to start. name: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: [\"v*.*.*\"]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  Release-Build:\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.runner }}\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      attestations: write\n      id-token: write\n    container:\n      image: ${{ matrix.container }}\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        include:\n          # x86_64 GNU builds on AlmaLinux 8 (glibc 2.28)\n          - runner: ubuntu-latest\n            target: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\n            container: almalinux:8\n            arch: x86_64\n          \n          # aarch64 GNU builds on AlmaLinux 8 (glibc 2.28)\n          - runner: ubuntu-latest-arm64\n            target: aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\n            container: almalinux:8\n            arch: aarch64\n          \n          # x86_64 musl builds (static binaries)\n          - runner: ubuntu-latest\n            target: x86_64-unknown-linux-musl\n            container: alpine:latest\n            arch: x86_64\n          \n          # aarch64 musl builds (static binaries)\n          - runner: ubuntu-latest-arm64\n            target: aarch64-unknown-linux-musl\n            container: alpine:latest\n            arch: aarch64\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Install dependencies (AlmaLinux)\n        if: ${{ contains(matrix.container, 'almalinux') }}\n        run: |\n          dnf install -y gcc gcc-c++ make git curl tar gzip\n\n      - name: Install dependencies (Alpine)\n        if: ${{ contains(matrix.container, 'alpine') }}\n        run: |\n          apk add --no-cache gcc g++ make git curl tar gzip musl-dev\n\n      - name: Install Rust\n        run: |\n          curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y --default-toolchain stable\n          echo \"$HOME/.cargo/bin\" >> $GITHUB_PATH\n\n      - name: Add Rust target\n        run: |\n          . \"$HOME/.cargo/env\"\n          rustup target add ${{ matrix.target }}\n\n      - name: Checkout repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Cargo build\n        run: |\n          . \"$HOME/.cargo/env\"\n          cargo build --features=cli --release --target ${{ matrix.target }}\n\n      - name: Check that pharos version matches the tag\n        run: python .github/scripts/tag_check.py \"${{ github.ref_name }}\"\n\n      - name: Archive\n        run: |\n          mkdir -p artifacts\n          cp -av target/${{ matrix.target }}/release/pharos .\n          tar -czf ${{ github.event.repository.name }}-${{ github.ref_name }}-${{ matrix.target }}.tar.gz pharos\n\n      - name: Attest Build Provenance\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@v1\n        continue-on-error: true\n        with:\n          subject-path: ${{ github.event.repository.name }}-${{ github.ref_name }}-${{ matrix.target }}.*\n\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          name: ${{ github.event.repository.name }}-${{ github.ref_name }}-${{ matrix.target }}\n          path: ${{ github.event.repository.name }}-${{ github.ref_name }}-${{ matrix.target }}.*\n          if-no-files-found: error\n          retention-days: 7\n\n  Release:\n    needs: [Release-Build]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Ensure artifacts dir exists\n        run: mkdir -p artifacts\n\n      - name: Download Artifact\n        uses: actions/download-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          path: artifacts\n          merge-multiple: true\n\n      - name: Release\n        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@c062e08bd532815e2082a85e87e3ef29c3e6d191\n        with:\n          name: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n          tag_name: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n          generate_release_notes: true\n          fail_on_unmatched_files: true\n          body: |\n            Welcome to this new release of pharos ${{ github.ref_name }}!\n\n            All artifacts are signed with this repos identity using Sigstore.\n            You can verify the signatures using the `GitHub` CLI.\n```shell\n            gh attestation verify --owner ${{ github.repository_owner }} <my-artifact>\n```\n            \n            **Build targets:**\n            - `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`: Built on AlmaLinux 8 (glibc 2.28) for broad compatibility\n            - `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`: Built on AlmaLinux 8 (glibc 2.28) for ARM64 systems\n            - `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`: Statically linked binary for maximum portability\n            - `aarch64-unknown-linux-musl`: Statically linked binary for ARM64 systems\n          token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref, '-pre') }}\n          files: artifacts/*"},"uuid":"eac9126d-8381-4330-bfa6-e124a4f271e5","timestamp":"2025-10-18T13:19:35.501Z","thinkingMetadata":{"level":"none","disabled":true,"triggers":[]}}
