1.0-test2`, `test3`, etc.\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 3: Add Second Architecture**\nSame as before - expand to aarch64\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 4: Add Version Check Script**\nSame as before\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 5: Add Build Attestation**\nSame as before\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 6: Add GitHub Release Creation**\nThis is where we actually create releases - by this point the build process is solid\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 7: Add musl Targets**\nSame as before\n\n---\n\n## Tag Management Strategy\n\n**For iteration (Phases 1-5)**:\n```bash\n# Create test tag\ngit tag v0.1.0-test1\ngit push origin v0.1.0-test1\n\n# Watch the workflow\ngh run watch\n\n# Clean up after testing\ngit tag -d v0.1.0-test1\ngit push origin :refs/tags/v0.1.0-test1\n\n# Next iteration\ngit tag v0.1.0-test2\ngit push origin v0.1.0-test2\n# ... etc\n```\n\n**For final release (Phase 6+)**:\n```bash\n# Create real release tag\ngit tag v0.1.0\ngit push origin v0.1.0\n# This will create an actual GitHub release\n```\n\nThis approach lets us:\n- Test the build process without creating GitHub releases\n- Iterate rapidly with test tags that we can delete\n- Only create real releases once everything works\n\nDoes this revised approach make sense? Should I proceed with Phase 1?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1804,"cache_read_input_tokens":18409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1804,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":865,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CUEjceHhmvfU7LVBvTXBY","type":"assistant","uuid":"f896dc2f-ed75-482d-8ca5-20bc4f87a721","timestamp":"2025-10-18T13:23:11.514Z"}
