{"parentUuid":"eeacaa46-5014-4272-9ad8-c2535fb84e37","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/devin/repos/a2-ai/test-build-processes","sessionId":"07c0d90e-4e54-4832-897c-75001749ff8a","version":"2.0.22","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NL7apStScHL4o93CW4yFqZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"github actions arm64 runner label ubuntu-24.04-arm 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Linux arm64 hosted runners now available for free in public repositories (Public Preview) - GitHub Changelog\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/changelog/2025-01-16-linux-arm64-hosted-runners-now-available-for-free-in-public-repositories-public-preview/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Actions Adds Linux ARM64 Hosted Runners in Public Preview - InfoQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/02/github-actions-linux-arm64/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Actions: Ubuntu 24.04 image now available for arm64 runners - GitHub Changelog\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/changelog/2024-06-24-github-actions-ubuntu-24-04-image-now-available-for-arm64-runners/\"},{\"title\":\"Linux arm64 hosted runners now available for free in public repositories (Public Preview) 🎉 · community · Discussion #148648\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/148648\"},{\"title\":\"Add runner \\\"ubuntu-latest-arm\\\" · community · Discussion #149392\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/149392\"},{\"title\":\"Add `ubuntu-22.04-arm` and `ubuntu-24.04-arm` to `runs-on` · Issue #504 · rhysd/actionlint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/504\"},{\"title\":\"Using ARM-based GitHub Actions Runners for Workflows - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/pradumnasaraf/using-arm-based-github-actions-runners-for-workflows-l6o\"},{\"title\":\"Arm64 on GitHub Actions: Powering faster, more efficient build systems - The GitHub Blog\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/arm64-on-github-actions-powering-faster-more-efficient-build-systems/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub-hosted runners reference - GitHub Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners\"},{\"title\":\"How can i specify the architecture in Github Actions? - Stack Overflow\",\"url\":\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/71217505/how-can-i-specify-the-architecture-in-github-actions\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about GitHub Actions ARM64 runners with the `ubuntu-24.04-arm` label in 2025:\n\n## Linux ARM64 Hosted Runners (Public Preview - January 2025)\n\nGitHub announced that Linux arm64 hosted runners are now available for free in public repositories, with labels `ubuntu-24.04-arm` and `ubuntu-22.04-arm`. This was released on January 16, 2025.\n\n### Key Details:\n\n**Usage:**\nThese labels will not work in private repositories, and the workflow will fail if added. To use them, you need to set the value for `runs-on:` as `ubuntu-24.04-arm` or `ubuntu-22.04-arm`.\n\n**Partnership:**\nIn partnership with Arm, GitHub provides the Ubuntu VM images for these runners.\n\n**Limitations:**\nWhile the arm64 runners are in public preview, you may experience longer queue times during peak usage hours.\n\n**Concurrency:**\nAll runs in public repositories will adhere to standard runners usage limits, with maximum concurrencies based on your plan type.\n\n**Software and Support:**\nThe Runner Image reports as `ubuntu-24.04-arm` and the included software links to the partner-runner-images repository.\n\n**Note:** There is currently no `ubuntu-latest-arm` label available, as discussed in the GitHub community forums."}]},"uuid":"1746c8fd-acc3-420a-b13b-af39779d01d4","timestamp":"2025-10-18T13:51:09.630Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"github actions arm64 runner label ubuntu-24.04-arm 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AeJAVJULs5YGJQbagqGB5N","content":[{"title":"Linux arm64 hosted runners now available for free in public repositories (Public Preview) - GitHub Changelog","url":"https://github.blog/changelog/2025-01-16-linux-arm64-hosted-runners-now-available-for-free-in-public-repositories-public-preview/"},{"title":"GitHub Actions Adds Linux ARM64 Hosted Runners in Public Preview - InfoQ","url":"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/02/github-actions-linux-arm64/"},{"title":"GitHub Actions: Ubuntu 24.04 image now available for arm64 runners - GitHub Changelog","url":"https://github.blog/changelog/2024-06-24-github-actions-ubuntu-24-04-image-now-available-for-arm64-runners/"},{"title":"Linux arm64 hosted runners now available for free in public repositories (Public Preview) 🎉 · community · Discussion #148648","url":"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/148648"},{"title":"Add runner \"ubuntu-latest-arm\" · community · Discussion #149392","url":"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/149392"},{"title":"Add `ubuntu-22.04-arm` and `ubuntu-24.04-arm` to `runs-on` · Issue #504 · rhysd/actionlint","url":"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/504"},{"title":"Using ARM-based GitHub Actions Runners for Workflows - DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/pradumnasaraf/using-arm-based-github-actions-runners-for-workflows-l6o"},{"title":"Arm64 on GitHub Actions: Powering faster, more efficient build systems - The GitHub Blog","url":"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/arm64-on-github-actions-powering-faster-more-efficient-build-systems/"},{"title":"GitHub-hosted runners reference - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners"},{"title":"How can i specify the architecture in Github Actions? - Stack Overflow","url":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/71217505/how-can-i-specify-the-architecture-in-github-actions"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about GitHub Actions ARM64 runners with the `ubuntu-24.04-arm` label in 2025:\n\n## Linux ARM64 Hosted Runners (Public Preview - January 2025)\n\nGitHub announced that Linux arm64 hosted runners are now available for free in public repositories, with labels `ubuntu-24.04-arm` and `ubuntu-22.04-arm`. This was released on January 16, 2025.\n\n### Key Details:\n\n**Usage:**\nThese labels will not work in private repositories, and the workflow will fail if added. To use them, you need to set the value for `runs-on:` as `ubuntu-24.04-arm` or `ubuntu-22.04-arm`.\n\n**Partnership:**\nIn partnership with Arm, GitHub provides the Ubuntu VM images for these runners.\n\n**Limitations:**\nWhile the arm64 runners are in public preview, you may experience longer queue times during peak usage hours.\n\n**Concurrency:**\nAll runs in public repositories will adhere to standard runners usage limits, with maximum concurrencies based on your plan type.\n\n**Software and Support:**\nThe Runner Image reports as `ubuntu-24.04-arm` and the included software links to the partner-runner-images repository.\n\n**Note:** There is currently no `ubuntu-latest-arm` label available, as discussed in the GitHub community forums."],"durationSeconds":14.343809207999845}}
